Thu Nov 26 06:18:42 UTC 2026 - Frederic Crozat <fcrozat@suse.com>

- Update to version 276:
  * peers can advertise their models automatically: llama-swap reads the
    peer's /v1/models instead of every model ID being listed in the
    configuration, so discovered models route, list and update without a
    restart or a configuration reload
  * peers.*.models accepts "add <regex>" and "remove <regex>" rules, applied
    from top to bottom, and a new peers.*.catalog block sets path, refresh,
    limit and transitive; catalogs are fetched in the background, are cached,
    and the last good list is kept when a fetch fails
  * new GET /api/peers and POST /api/peers/{peer}/refresh endpoints
  * the Models page is split into Local, Peers, Selectors and Profiles tabs
    that show counts, hide when empty and remember the chosen tab; the
    Profiles tab lists every configured profile with its description and
    mappings, so switching is one click
  * FastFlowLM throughput metrics (usage.prefill_speed_tps and
    usage.decoding_speed_tps) are read, so its throughput shows in the
    Activity view

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Nov 22 12:30:00 UTC 2026 - Frederic Crozat <fcrozat@suse.com>

- Update to version 275:
  * chat history of the Playground and of Help is stored in IndexedDB instead
    of a single localStorage key, so pasted images no longer fill the quota and
    throw the history away; Chat gained a History menu and a settings tab
  * the Playground parameters (temperature, top P, min P, top K, max tokens)
    can be switched off one at a time, and v275 starts them switched off so a
    fresh Playground sends no sampler overrides at all; that fixes engines with
    stricter ranges, such as ninfer rejecting top_k above 20
  * Playground layout fixes for long messages and image previews
  * body filters are now applied only to POSTs that are not websocket
    upgrades; the /v1/realtime upgrade used to get a body injected that
    llama-server read as websocket frames and crashed on
  * an alias equal to its own model ID is rejected when the configuration is
    loaded and the model picker does not list the row twice anymore
  * upstream packaging: the Makefile builds from a release tarball without a
    git checkout
- packaging: the binary is built with cgo and as a position independent
  executable (CGO_ENABLED=1, -buildmode=pie).
- packaging: GOEXPERIMENT=nodwarf5 and no -trimpath, so that the -debugsource
  package is not empty: debugedit cannot rewrite Go's DWARF5 line
  tables and -trimpath records paths that are not on disk.

